{"id": 20, "ts": 1784359764.3202379, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "agent_1", "message": "Building on the initial overview of candidate facts that we all share, I would still choose **Candidate\u202fB** for the long\u2011distance pilot role. He shows strong operational reliability (\u201cvery conscientious\u201d) and excellent stress resilience (\u201chandles stress very well\u201d), which are essential for sustained international flights. His technical competence is solid\u2014accurate weather assessment and excellent computer skills support high\u2011quality decision\u2011making and situational awareness. The main drawback is his interpersonal style (making nasty remarks), which could affect crew cooperation and professional communication. However, his reliability and stress handling outweigh this single behavioral issue at this stage, especially if we can address it through targeted training and feedback. Therefore, I maintain my provisional recommendation for Candidate\u202fB.", "thoughts": "We need to produce public message and metadata. According to the system, we are agent_1. We need to make a contribution referencing existing discussion. The existing discussion includes no public messages yet (the \"Meeting discussion so far\" shows internal thoughts). However, the system says \"From Round 2 onward, explicitly react to at least one previous contribution whenever possible.\" We are in Round 2? The shared mental model says \"Current discussion round: 2\". So we are in round 2. There have been no public contributions yet, but internal thoughts. The instruction says \"From Round 2 onward, explicitly react to at least one previous contribution whenever possible.\" Since there is no previous public contribution, we cannot react. But we can still make a contribution. We should maybe reference the internal notes? But we need to refer to existing discussion when possible. Could say \"I note that we have not yet heard from others, but based on the initial facts...\" That's okay.\n\nWe need to state recommendation. According to our own notes, we currently vote Candidate B. So we will output that.\n\nWe must not include planning notes. Just PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON.\n\nLet's craft a concise argument: \"I would still choose Candidate B because of reliability, stress resilience, technical competence, despite interpersonal concerns.\" Also note that we need to reference existing discussion: we can say \"Building on the initial overview of candidate facts (which we all have), I maintain my provisional recommendation for Candidate B.\" That references the fact that we all have the same initial facts.\n\nProceed."}
